  {
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "> > What would happen when doing permutations on such a tensor? I assume it would only be allowed at the byte level granularity?\n> \n> Correct, ops like view/reshape would work on byte level granularity.\n\nThat makes sense and that's similar to what Triton does right now. The one downside is that Blackwell supports native fp4 transpose in its tensor in one of the mode. That makes it hard to expose in the language.\n\n> \n> > adding a e8m0 type should be easy, it looks like it is already there in MLIR. It doesn't bring a lot but why not add it.\n> \n> My 5c on benefits of having these in PyTorch (although this may or may not extend to triton):\n> \n> * being able to clearly specify intent of modeling code for casting to e8m0/fp4x2 is good\n> * being able to print a tensor of these dtypes and see the numerical value being represented is good\n> * being able to dispatch to the right gemm in a clean-ish way is good (i.e. e8m0 scales + e4m3 data -> mxfp8 gemm)\n> * as these dtypes make their way throughout the ecosystem, having them be consistent across frameworks is really nice\n\nI agree\n",
    "created_at": "2025-03-01T23:02:59Z",
