  {
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "Hi @vkuzo :\n\nI tested the value of qdq in mxfp4 format for torchao as well as triton separately and found that the output is not consistent, here is my code as well as the output. Which output is golden for triton mxfp4 qdq please?\n\n```\nimport torch\nfrom torchao.prototype.mx_formats.mx_tensor import MXTensor\nfrom torchao.prototype.mx_formats.mx_tensor import ScaleCalculationMode\n\n# Note: MX int8 is not implemented yet  refer: https://github.com/pytorch/ao/tree/main/torchao/prototype/mx_formats\nfrom torchao.prototype.mx_formats.constants import DTYPE_FP6_E2M3, DTYPE_FP6_E3M2, DTYPE_FP4\n\n# Print PyTorch and CUDA environment information\nprint(\"PyTorch version:\", torch.__version__)\nprint(\"CUDA available:\", torch.cuda.is_available())\nif torch.cuda.is_available():\n    # torch.version.cuda is not a public attribute, but used here for demonstration\n    print(\"CUDA version:\", torch.version.cuda)\n    print(\"Number of GPUs:\", torch.cuda.device_count())\n    for i in range(torch.cuda.device_count()):\n        print(f\"GPU {i} name:\", torch.cuda.get_device_name(i))\ntry:\n    import triton\n    print(\"Triton version:\", triton.__version__)\nexcept ImportError:\n    print(\"Triton is not installed\")\n\n# Construct a test tensor with multiple groups of typical values for quantization testing\nvalues = [6, 0, 0.24, 0.25, 0.75, 0.99, 1.2, 1.3] * 4  # Repeat 4 times, length 32\nx = torch.tensor(values, dtype=torch.bfloat16, device=\"cuda\").view(1, -1)\n\n# elem_dtype can be torch.float8_e4m3fn, torch.float8_e5m2, DTYPE_FP6_E2M3, DTYPE_FP6_E3M2, torch.float4_e2m1fn_x2\nelem_dtype = DTYPE_FP4\n\n# Quantize from high precision to MX format, block size defaults to 32\nx_torchao_mxfp4 = MXTensor.to_mx(x, elem_dtype, scaling_mode=ScaleCalculationMode.FLOOR)\n# Dequantize MX format back to high precision\nx_torchao_mxfp4 = x_torchao_mxfp4.to_dtype(torch.bfloat16)\n\n# refer: https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/blob/main/python/triton_kernels/triton_kernels/numerics_details/mxfp.py\nfrom mx_triton import downcast_to_mxfp, upcast_from_mxfp, DequantScaleRoundingMode\n# Quantize using Triton kernel\nx_triton_mxfp4, scale, _ = downcast_to_mxfp(\n    x, torch.uint8, axis=-1, DEQUANT_SCALE_ROUNDING_MODE=DequantScaleRoundingMode.ROUND_DOWN, swizzle_axis=None\n)\n# Dequantize using Triton kernel\nx_triton_mxfp4 = upcast_from_mxfp(x_triton_mxfp4, scale, x.dtype, axis=-1, swizzle_axis=None)\n\n# Print the sum of the dequantized tensors for comparison\nprint(x_torchao_mxfp4.sum())\nprint(x_triton_mxfp4.sum())\n\n# Assert that the two dequantized results are close\ntorch.testing.assert_close(x_triton_mxfp4, x_torchao_mxfp4)\n\n\n# Output\nPyTorch version: 2.7.0+cu126\nCUDA available: True\nCUDA version: 12.6\nNumber of GPUs: 8\nGPU 0 name: NVIDIA A100-SXM4-80GB\nGPU 1 name: NVIDIA A100-SXM4-80GB\nGPU 2 name: NVIDIA A100-SXM4-80GB\nGPU 3 name: NVIDIA A100-SXM4-80GB\nGPU 4 name: NVIDIA A100-SXM4-80GB\nGPU 5 name: NVIDIA A100-SXM4-80GB\nGPU 6 name: NVIDIA A100-SXM4-80GB\nGPU 7 name: NVIDIA A100-SXM4-80GB\nTriton version: 3.3.0\ntensor(42., device='cuda:0', dtype=torch.bfloat16)\ntensor(44., device='cuda:0', dtype=torch.bfloat16)\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/share_data/users/chuhao/project/vllm_online_quant/torchmo/tests/test_mx_quantization_kernel.py\", line 313, in <module>\n    torch.testing.assert_close(x_triton_mxfp4, x_torchao_mxfp4)\n  File \"/share_data/users/chuhao/miniconda3/envs/torchmo/lib/python3.12/site-packages/torch/testing/_comparison.py\", line 1519, in assert_close\n    raise error_metas[0].to_error(msg)\nAssertionError: Tensor-likes are not close!\n\nMismatched elements: 4 / 32 (12.5%)\nGreatest absolute difference: 0.5 at index (0, 3) (up to 1e-05 allowed)\nGreatest relative difference: inf at index (0, 3) (up to 0.016 allowed)\n```",
